  "CardDescription": {
    "ParentObjectID": "cmcBrambleThicket",
    "LocalizationKey": "CMC_BrambleThicket_CardDescription",
    "DefaultText": "In the heat of summer the brambles have run wild across the trail between Stillwater Meadow and Sett Warren, a wall of thorny canes too dense to walk through. Cut a way through with a sickle to clear the path quickly, or tear through it with your bare hands if you have no blade - slower, but it works. Once cut back, the trail stays open for the rest of the summer."
  },
